    <statement><p>Evaluate the double integral
 <m>\displaystyle \iint_D \cos\sqrt{x^2+y^2} dA,</m>
where <m>D</m> is the disc with center the origin and radius <m>6,</m> by changing to polar coordinates.</p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\pi \mathopen{}\left(6\sin\mathopen{}\left(6\right)+\cos\mathopen{}\left(6\right)-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
